      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Meryetyotes|702311\", \"verdict\": \"same_name\", \"reasoning\": \"The transliteration Mr.yt-jtj=s reads as the signs m, r, y, t, j, t, j, s. In Meryetyotes, M stands for m. The first e is an extra vowel letter. r stands for r, y for y, and the second e is another extra vowel letter. t stands for t, the feminine ending of Meryt, which is written here. The next y stands for the first j, which a modern spelling may write as i or y. The o is an extra vowel letter. The following t stands for the t of jtj. The second j is left out, which is allowed. The last e is an extra vowel letter, and s stands for s from =s. Every sign is matched in order and no consonant of record 1 is left over, so the two are the same name.\"}"
